---
import DefaultLayout from "@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro"
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro"
---

<DefaultLayout title="Eduardo Torres Dávila: Data Science">
  <div class="mt-24 mb-12 m-6 sm:mx-12 lg:mx-0">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
      <h1 class="text-blue text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-display">Data Science</h1>
      <div class="gap-6 flex">
        <a href="/">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-house hover:opacity-70"></i>
        </a>
        <a href="/mathematics">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus hover:text-red"></i>
        </a>
        <a href="/software">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-code hover:text-green"></i>
        </a>
        <a>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-database text-blue"></i>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="mb-3 indent-4 mx-6 sm:mx-12 lg:mx-0">
    A recent journey for me has been into the field of data science. As someone
    who enjoys both mathematical rigor and software engineering challenges, I'm
    drawn to the way data science provides a middle ground between the two. It
    allows me to leverage my years of advanced mathematical training while
    solving real-world problems through software. Python is my language of
    choice, with a focus on libraries such as <a class="text-blue underline
      decoration-2" href="https://pandas.pydata.org/">Pandas</a>, <a
      class="text-blue underline decoration-2"
      href="https://scikit-learn.org/stable/">scikit-learn</a>, <a
      class="text-blue underline decoration-2"
      href="https://numpy.org/">NumPy</a>, and <a class="text-blue underline
      decoration-2" href="https://matplotlib.org/">Matplotlib</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-12 indent-4 mx-6 sm:mx-12 lg:mx-0">
    In the summer of 2025, I participated in the <a class="text-blue underline
      decoration-2" href="https://cse.umn.edu/ima/math-industry-boot-camp">IMA
      Math-to-Industry Boot Camp</a>. During the first three weeks I took short
    courses in statistical modeling, machine learning, and optimization. The
    last three weeks were devoted to company sponsored projects where I worked
    with four teammates on a U.S. Bank project that modeled mortgage-backed
    security price curves. We used linear regression and machine learning on
    large financial datasets to build parsimonious models that improved pricing
    predictions.
  </p>
